# Claude Code reads a skill's frontmatter from SKILL.md, and the description is the whole
# matching surface. Observed 2026-08-28: with the file CRLF the session skill list shows the
# H1 instead of the description; with it LF the description resolves. core.autocrlf=true is
# set on the Windows dev machine and there is no other .gitattributes, so every checkout
# rewrote it CRLF. Pin these files to LF.
#
# Deliberately scoped to this one pattern. No `* text=auto`, so nothing already committed
# renormalizes. The pattern is a glob rather than the single path because the only reason
# .claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md never hit this is .gitignore:24 excluding it, so the
# next tracked skill would inherit the problem.
.claude/skills/**/SKILL.md text eol=lf

# Rules files are frontmatter-parsed exactly as SKILL.md is, and the 2026-08-28
# observation above applies unchanged: a CRLF frontmatter block does not resolve.
.claude/rules/**/*.md text eol=lf
